Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.50,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.02,0:00:07.69,Default,,0,0,900,,Angels and demons were circling over me,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.69,0:00:13.40,Default,,0,0,900,,Crossing a brambly path of stars and milky ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.10,0:00:19.07,Default,,0,0,900,,He who does not perceive his calling,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.90,0:00:25.48,Default,,0,0,900,,does not know true happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.08,0:00:31.28,Default,,0,0,900,,Watch in awe! Watch in awe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.85,0:00:37.02,Default,,0,0,900,,Flying in glory, Flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.62,0:00:42.83,Default,,0,0,900,,Watch in awe! Watch in awe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.03,0:00:48.23,Default,,0,0,900,,Flying in glory, Flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.33,0:01:00.58,Default,,0,0,900,,I am calling, calling now.\NSpirits rise and falling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.05,0:01:06.05,Default,,0,0,900,,To be with you longer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.32,0:01:12.36,Default,,0,0,900,,Calling, calling...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.39,0:01:17.86,Default,,0,0,900,,in the depth of longing
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.33,0:01:23.83,Default,,0,0,900,,To stay myself longer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.83,0:01:29.24,Default,,0,0,900,,The flow may swallow you, flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.15,0:01:52.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Aramaki-San, my sincere apologies\Nfor making you come all the way here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.86,0:01:56.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Now that Undersecretary of Foreign Affairs\NKim has received an assassination threat,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.45,0:01:58.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,the situation falls under our jurisdiction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.03,0:02:04.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Moreover, you graciously provided us with\Ncritical information in an earlier matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.75,0:02:10.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Undersecretary has arrived\Nin Kagoshima on schedule.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.04,0:02:12.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We have waited for five long years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.34,0:02:17.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Undersecretary Kim is the first high-profile government\Nofficial to pay a visit to honour war casualties
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.26,0:02:21.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,after permission was granted to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.85,0:02:25.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Aramaki-San, I ask that you provide\Nthe best possible protection.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.64,0:02:26.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.14,0:02:29.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then I will leave it in your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.40,0:02:39.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Batou, you have temporary command here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.28,0:02:42.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What?! You have a personal errand\Nat an important time like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.78,0:02:44.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'll be back by nightfall.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.58,0:02:47.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Saitou, Pazu, and Bomer, stay with Batou.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.37,0:02:52.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Coordinate closely with the Major\Nas she tries to track down who made the threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.21,0:02:55.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.80,0:02:59.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,To pay my respects to a friend on the\Nseventh anniversary of his funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.68,0:03:05.57,Default,,500,0,500,,Assassination \N Duet
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.35,0:03:12.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You're late.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.02,0:03:17.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Just before you arrived, many of Tsujisaki's\Nacquaintances paid their respects.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.74,0:03:19.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Is that so? I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.91,0:03:32.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Effective treatment for cyberbrain\Nscleroses did not exist back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.00,0:03:32.92,Default,,0,0,900,,{\i1}Tsujisaki Clan{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.54,0:03:38.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Those who will be sorely missed\Ntend to pass away earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.76,0:03:45.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,True. Of the three of us, Tsujisaki was the\None who was most favoured by Colonel Tonoda.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.97,0:03:49.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I know how you feel about the Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.81,0:03:56.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I only did as the Colonel ordered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.32,0:03:58.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's just like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.95,0:04:04.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ah, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.45,0:04:06.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.45,0:04:07.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'll return immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.08,0:04:11.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm sorry, but I have to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.46,0:04:12.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.93,0:04:29.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If I remember correctly, you are Tsujisaki's...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.22,0:04:32.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes, I'm Saori.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.56,0:04:37.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm sure that my father is glad\Nto have you here, Aramaki-San.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.94,0:04:43.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He said that you helped him in many\Nways during my mother's funeral rites.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.45,0:04:47.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You were still a student back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.74,0:04:51.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I believe you also had a younger brother\Nin elementary school, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.83,0:04:52.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.04,0:04:58.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Um... There's something I'd like to ask you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.84,0:04:59.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,And that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.96,0:05:02.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's about my brother, Yuu.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.05,0:05:07.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He has suddenly begun acting like my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.89,0:05:13.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He was raised well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.81,0:05:16.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He resembles Tsujisaki, when he was young.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.02,0:05:19.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No, that's not what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.98,0:05:21.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's not just a physical resemblance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.69,0:05:24.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Both his voice and manner of speech\Nare now quite similar to our father's.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.61,0:05:26.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Does that pose some kind of problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.99,0:05:33.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He recently began to access military news sites,\Nthough he has never shown any interest before now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.70,0:05:40.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In addition, I sometimes wake up in the night\Nbecause I hear a noise in the living room.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.00,0:05:45.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and I find my brother sitting there\Nreading my father's books very intently.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.80,0:05:49.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I don't even know when he sleeps,\Nsince this has been occurring nightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.39,0:05:55.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Now that you mention it,\NI could never tell when Tsujisaki slept, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.60,0:05:59.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes. When I became worried and\Nasked him what he was doing,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.52,0:06:05.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,all he did was to look at me and\Nask, "Saori, you're still awake?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.99,0:06:07.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.82,0:06:11.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It seems like he is contacting\Nsomeone a lot lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.12,0:06:15.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But he won't tell me who,\Nno matter how many times I ask him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.29,0:06:20.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Large packages from overseas keep arriving too...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.92,0:06:24.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Do you think it's possible that he\Nmight be involved in something strange?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.59,0:06:31.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Please, I want you to investigate\Nwhy he changed so suddenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.85,0:06:42.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm very sorry, but I cannot use my professional\Nauthority for private matters like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.23,0:06:48.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You may confide in me, but I cannot help\Nyou based on what you have told me so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.03,0:06:52.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's true, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.74,0:06:54.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.54,0:06:59.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I heard that you were a good friend\Nof my father's, so I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.54,0:07:03.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Tsujisaki was not a friend,\Nhe was just a comrade-in-arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.60,0:07:20.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.19,0:07:22.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes, I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.11,0:07:24.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'll do it right, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.48,0:07:27.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I know...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.16,0:07:40.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Chinese Undersecretary of Foreign\NAffairs, Kim, arrived today.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.96,0:07:44.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He plans to pay homage to\NKagoshima's war casualties tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.46,0:07:47.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Since many Chinese who were\Nliving in Okinawa at the time
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.84,0:07:51.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,were interred in the memorial\Nmonolith alongside the Japanese,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.63,0:07:54.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,the Chinese government has expressed\Nits desire to pay an official visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.85,0:07:58.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Japanese government issued special\Npermission for this particular visit;
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.43,0:08:02.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,the culmination of this is\NUndersecretary Kim's visit to Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.23,0:08:10.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In addition, the police appear to have heightened security\Nmeasures in place due to increased protests by the Japanese.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.44,0:08:14.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Old Man is purposefully\Nletting himself be seen on TV.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.45,0:08:15.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How easygoing of him...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.33,0:08:20.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,An here we are laying low,\Ntoiling away in our pursuit of the suspect...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.46,0:08:23.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Any clues as to the target's identity?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.54,0:08:27.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm, well... This just came in.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.76,0:08:34.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is the assassin who is\Ntargeting Undersecretary Kim?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.43,0:08:37.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,After analysing the Undersecretary's schedule,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.06,0:08:41.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,we reached the conclusion that the\Nassassin would probably be a sniper.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.06,0:08:44.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Using that assumption to narrow\Ndown our list of suspects,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.35,0:08:46.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,we found evidence that a\Nsophisticated sniper rifle had been
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.94,0:08:49.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,carefully disassembled and shipped in\Nas separate parts via the Etorofu route.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.73,0:08:52.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,From there, we determined the\Naddressee of the packages,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.74,0:08:59.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and the individual who came to pick up the packages that\Nhad been sent to P.O. boxes at different locations...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.04,0:09:01.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,is that person there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.25,0:09:04.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm having the system run an\Nidentity check using this image,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.83,0:09:07.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but it will take about two more\Nhours for the results to come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.25,0:09:10.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Have you determined the identity of the suspect?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.55,0:09:13.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We haven't reached a final conclusion,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.13,0:09:16.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but judging from the circumstances,\Nhe is our best candidate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.35,0:09:19.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Someone you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.39,0:09:30.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Tsujisaki Yuu, son of the former chief of\NGSDF Intelligence, Colonel Tsujisaki Hideo,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.42,0:09:51.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I told you, I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.71,0:09:54.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.02,0:09:59.93,Default,,0,320,700,,{\i1}Kim, the Undersecretary of Foreign\NAffairs, Will Visit the Memorial Monument{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.05,0:09:57.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I have to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.84,0:10:00.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's to avenge my mother's...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.85,0:10:03.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ritsuko's death, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.19,0:10:08.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Isn't that right, Yuu?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.55,0:10:40.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Stay quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.56,0:10:47.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Major, we missed him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.85,0:10:49.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He already left.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.52,0:10:52.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm sorry to visit at this ungodly hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.73,0:10:55.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ishikawa, he knew we were coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.23,0:10:57.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Run a check on all transportation\Nmonitors immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.44,0:10:58.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.74,0:11:00.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Y-You are...?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.53,0:11:01.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I work under Aramaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.03,0:11:03.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Under Aramaki-San...?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.45,0:11:04.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.33,0:11:06.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,To get straight to the point,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.45,0:11:10.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,we came here to detain your\Nbrother, Tsujisaki Yuu.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.54,0:11:13.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Detain... Detain Yuu?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.13,0:11:16.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He already left the premises.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.63,0:11:20.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,At least knock, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.34,0:11:21.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is the room of a lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.05,0:11:23.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.85,0:11:26.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Major, I found this on his desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.35,0:11:29.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What has Yuu done?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.64,0:11:34.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You know of Undersecretary of Foreign Affairs,\NKim, who is currently visiting Japan, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.15,0:11:37.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,There has been a threat against his life,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.86,0:11:43.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and your brother is the number one suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.45,0:11:44.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.74,0:11:53.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,While we don't know his motives, we have confirmed that\Nhe has hacked into Colonel Tsujisaki's SDF data library.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.42,0:11:59.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The records indicate that he accessed it starting\Non the day after his birthday until yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.59,0:12:01.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The reason why his intrusion\Nwent undetected until now
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.01,0:12:06.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,is that he opened the maintenance\Nfirewall using the proper "keys".
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.10,0:12:09.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yuu did such things...?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.10,0:12:12.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How long has your brother been\Nusing the portable terminal?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.69,0:12:20.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yuu received a package containing the portable\Nterminal our father used on his sixteenth birthday.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.99,0:12:26.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When Yuu was little, it perplexed my\Nfather that Yuu really wanted the terminal.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.28,0:12:30.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,At the time, my father promised Yuu that\Nhe'd give him the terminal when Yuu grew up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.00,0:12:35.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The password for the maintenance firewall\Nmust have been stored in the terminal.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.50,0:12:38.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We are trying to access the library ourselves,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.50,0:12:41.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but cracking the password is proving\Ndifficult and will require several hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.38,0:12:46.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,At this point, only your\Nbrother knows what is in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.72,0:12:50.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He has been fascinated with\Nit since it was delivered.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.89,0:12:52.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He won't tell me anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.02,0:12:55.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In any case, I wonder where\Nhe is at this time of night...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.02,0:12:57.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Considering that he is no longer here,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.11,0:13:02.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,we should assume that he has entered\Nthe final stages of the assassination.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.49,0:13:05.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Please stop my brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.70,0:13:07.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Please don't let him become a murderer!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.99,0:13:09.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's why we're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.13,0:13:21.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:22.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Did you find something?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.92,0:13:27.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,There is no sign of him on the monitors\Nat train stations and airports at present.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.85,0:13:32.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,However, something about\NColonel Tsujisaki caught my eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.73,0:13:34.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Something about Colonel Tsujisaki?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.14,0:13:38.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's something I heard while I was\Nstill working with the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.44,0:13:41.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Our Chief, the current Chief of\NGSDF Intelligence, Kubota and
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.65,0:13:46.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Colonel Tsujisaki used to be called\N"The Three Crows of the Tonoda School."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.74,0:13:53.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In particular, Colonel Tsujisaki was respected by his peers,\Nand his course for new members received special accolades.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.62,0:13:56.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,From sharpshooting to disarming explosives,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.25,0:14:00.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,hand-to-hand combat,\Nweapons acquisition and even covert ops...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.46,0:14:05.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It is said that he thought a wide range of\Nskills was important and cultivated many experts.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.43,0:14:09.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,From here on, it is only speculation on my part,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.35,0:14:15.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but consider Tsujisaki Yuu's action thus far and the degree\Nof cunning in his apparent ability to predict our movements.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.56,0:14:17.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If you put the two together...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.06,0:14:23.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,His father's library was a collection of war\Ntactics that had been accumulated over the years,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.03,0:14:31.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and Tsujisaki Yuu succeeded in secretly obtaining that\Ninformation by using the password in his father's terminal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.53,0:14:38.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In other words, his mind is now that of an assassin who has\Nbeen trained by an extremely capable intelligence officer?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.04,0:14:40.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I do not have conclusive proof,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.63,0:14:44.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but considering how he was continued to brilliantly\Ncircumvent all efforts on our part to capture him,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.34,0:14:46.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,the possibility is high.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.93,0:14:54.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Batou, don't let the fact that he is the son of\Nmy old friend affect your operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.56,0:14:58.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Protecting Undersecretary\NKim is our foremost priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.06,0:15:00.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Don't think about anything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.36,0:15:03.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's not as if I didn't intend to do just\Nthat from the beginning, of course...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.86,0:15:09.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Chief, that may be true,\Nbut I will try to spare his life anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.03,0:15:11.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,However, in the worst-case scenario...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.95,0:15:12.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.95,0:15:21.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Chief Aramaki, there is a message from\Nthe GSDF with encryption code 839-0852.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.67,0:15:24.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's an old GSDF encryption code.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.25,0:15:27.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Decode and route it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.93,0:15:36.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It has been a long time\Nsince we last spoke, Aramaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.22,0:15:38.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Tsujisaki...?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.56,0:15:44.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What is this about?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.65,0:15:47.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,At first, I had no intention of doing anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.57,0:15:50.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I just wanted to tell "myself" the truth...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.16,0:15:54.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The truth that I would want\Npassed on to posterity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.45,0:15:56.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In order to do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.16,0:15:59.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I overwrote my memory onto my son's cyberbrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.75,0:16:05.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I never thought that would\Nmake me into an assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.34,0:16:10.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What did you hide in the data library?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.34,0:16:12.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The truth behind the Okinawa Incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.26,0:16:16.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I just wanted that truth to\Nbe passed on to posterity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.14,0:16:21.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But upon learning the truth,\N"I" learned the truth behind my mother's death,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.44,0:16:24.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and that only created a desire for vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.94,0:16:28.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is unexpected.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.44,0:16:31.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I did not even think once about assassination.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.95,0:16:36.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But I am no longer able to\Nstop "my" desire for vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.24,0:16:39.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Vengeance, after all these years?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.24,0:16:40.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's not like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.04,0:16:42.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.17,0:16:47.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But now, I'm Tsujisaki Hideo and\NTsujisaki Yuu at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.46,0:16:55.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Mingled memories now flow together in our consciousness,\Nand "I" act on my thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.05,0:16:58.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Or, is it the opposite?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.26,0:17:02.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When this is finished, it may be that I\Nwill become someone entirely different.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.64,0:17:05.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Do you intend to make your son into an assassin?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:08.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If it could at all help it, I would prefer not to.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.44,0:17:12.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But you know what? No one can stop this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.15,0:17:15.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It must be Yuu's youth that necessitates this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.24,0:17:19.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Take care of Saori for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.54,0:17:23.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It seems that I must have my vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.75,0:17:25.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Tsujisaki...!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.33,0:17:28.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm sorry, Aramaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.22,0:17:43.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Damn it, we can't even catch him using ID codes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.39,0:17:46.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Can't we just prevent general visitors\Nfrom entering the grounds?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.19,0:17:54.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Undersecretary Kim requested permission to have as many\Nassociates with him as possible to console the deceased.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.49,0:18:00.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, he's basically asking to be killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.49,0:18:04.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No matter the outcome,\Nit'll be a great performance, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.62,0:18:07.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Saitou, can you scope out possible sniping points?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.08,0:18:10.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He has a sniper rifle with\Nan extremely long range.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.42,0:18:14.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Even if he has disassembled it for\Nportability, it should still be quite obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.72,0:18:19.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If he's planning to make the kill as a sniper,\Nmy current location is the best position.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.60,0:18:23.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Other locations suffer from a\Nstrong sea breeze and obstructions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.68,0:18:25.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,He would not be able to shoot with any accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.61,0:18:36.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Heh, fishing in a time like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.28,0:18:38.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Bomer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.28,0:18:39.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.28,0:18:40.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Nothing here, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.70,0:18:45.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,According to the programme,\Nthe presentation of flowers is next.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.79,0:18:49.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's the best opportunity, since the SP\Nwill have to step away from his side.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.51,0:18:57.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Where is he?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.14,0:19:03.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Where is he targeting from?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.52,0:19:11.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We've found the weapon!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.02,0:19:13.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What about the sniper?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.36,0:19:16.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,There's no sign of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.24,0:19:21.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,All we've found is one sniper rifle\Nand a student whose uniform was taken.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.16,0:19:24.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, the rifle was a ruse!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.20,0:20:05.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Major, I didn't know that you were here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.70,0:20:09.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We were able to determine the\Nactual plot from Tsujisaki's data.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.83,0:20:12.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,According to him,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.71,0:20:17.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"The most effective assassination method is to approach\Nthe target without regard for an escape route."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.30,0:20:20.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,An assassin with a one-way ticket, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.77,0:20:31.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.09,0:21:10.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Undersecretary Kim safely completed all of his\Nplanned events and departed yesterday afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.60,0:21:13.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It was a risky operation,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.02,0:21:21.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but we could see no option other than to implant a\Nmemory that he succeeded in his quest for vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.57,0:21:26.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Unfortunately, he may not remember\Nyou even if he regains consciousness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.74,0:21:34.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It is quite possible that he is now a stranger\Nwho is neither your brother nor your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.67,0:21:41.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It does not matter...\Nas long as Yuu lives and stays by my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.55,0:21:50.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If anything happens, contact this number.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.27,0:21:57.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.99,0:22:08.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Using the data that the father left behind,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.37,0:22:12.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,the son reconstructed the father's memories and\Nattempted to have the two personalities coexist.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.08,0:22:16.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,As a result, each personality affected the other.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.29,0:22:20.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,However, I think that the procedure\Nerased Colonel Tsujisaki's memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.38,0:22:22.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In addition, while the possibility is remote,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.96,0:22:27.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,it is possible that he'll return to\Nbeing the boy named Tsujisaki Yuu.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.18,0:22:29.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.60,0:22:34.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,However, it is rather trying to lose\Na close friend twice in my old age.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.60,0:22:37.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I thought he was your comrade-in-arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.06,0:22:40.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.56,0:23:19.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She's so cold and human
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.44,0:23:22.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's something humans do
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.44,0:23:27.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She stays so cold in her soul, she's so number 9
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.74,0:23:30.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She's incredible math
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.74,0:23:35.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Just incredible math
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.20,0:23:39.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,And is she really human?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.62,0:23:42.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She says there's something new
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.50,0:23:47.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But wake a lithium flower, just about to bloom
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.63,0:23:50.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I smell lithium now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.34,0:23:55.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Smelling lithium now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.72,0:23:59.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How... is she what she doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.93,0:24:00.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.64,0:24:03.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How... is she what she doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.02,0:24:05.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.61,0:24:07.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How is she when she doesn't suffer
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.61,0:24:10.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I wonder what she does when she wakes up
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.11,0:24:14.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When she wakes up
